      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nHowever, the shaft in question where the incident had occurred was unsecured, neither it was welded nor secured by using screws."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e2e7bddcc9e2470f9b28350bca4ac69b_89",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "There is ample evidence on record in the form of replies of DLF and RWA that it was the maintenance company which was responsible for the maintenance and upkeep of the entire complex including the stilts, basement, fire exits as well as CR "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b2e639187c01474bbd299b8b947faad7_90",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nAccordingly, the prime responsibility for any untoward incident was that of maintenance company JLL."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "23981df128c24eeaacd4a18b4812d088_91",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Chargesheet also shows that after registration of FIR, when the place of incident was again visited, the iron sheets were affixed and the area was secured by JLL.\n19."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "cce68ba14e774249a69a39747a54ba6b_92",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The impugned order is completely a legal order and within the jurisdiction of Ld. MM."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c177c7f3261f47c29c047f2c01741a83_93",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "There is no illegality or infirmity in the same as simply the cognizance has been taken and the summons have been issued to chargesheeted accused persons."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a597b69008e5489eb0896657d5589374_94",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS",
        "explicit_leakage_phrase"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bset\\s+aside\\b",
          "matched_text": "set aside",
          "start": 74,
          "end": 83
        }
      ],
      "text_preview": "Revisional jurisdiction is limited in nature and impugned order cannot be set aside merely because another view is possible."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "41b1ff5e24904cbdb57a3acf8a2ef07f_95",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It has to be shown that an order is illegal, infirm, perverse or beyond the jurisdiction of Ld. Trial Court before it can be interfered with."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3ce252efd5d04de2b018eebe524c5516_96",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "However, in this case, there is no such illegality or infirmity in the impugned order ."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "dd3f916520e040d39f21e1dc878952ae_97",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nAs regards the grounds taken in the present revision petition, the same can be considered at the stage of arguments on charge."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0c31e42fa049448da1a106570a757e00_98",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Moreover, the responsibilities of the revisionist as Directors of M/s JLL can only be established at the stage of evidence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "449588c0c3c8484993f035b6431a2106_100",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In these circumstances, it is submitted that the present revision petitions are not maintainable and deserve to be dismissed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b56d41695f95444fa434efbb04f8882b_102",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Similarly, the decision in Pepsi Food's case (supra) is not applicable to the facts of the present case as it was an order passed in a quashing petition filed u/s 482 CrPC while CR No. 2192023 Audhesh Kumar Pandey Vs State CR No. 2202023 Ra"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c7c36a7434984373a4679af0ec6618db_103",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is held by the Apex Court in Kishan Lal Vs. Dharmender Bafna & Anr. Crl. No. 1283/2009 that a revisional court should not interfere with the discretionary jurisdiction exercised by Ld. Magistrate unless a jurisdictional error or an error"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f5a74414d07e4ca7ad93f7b63fa5784a_104",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "24. In the present case, the Revisionists have been summoned as accused to be tried for offence u/s 304A IPC."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b7eff90d9f034e8cadb19ed5d44cbd9f_105",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Sec. 304A IPC provides punishment for causing death by doing any rash or negligent act not amounting to culpable homicide."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7060198616b94ac6ba9eec5ee086e355_106",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "While rashness is acting in the hope that no mischievous consequences will ensue, though aware of the likelihood of such consequences; negligence is acting without the awareness that harmful or mischievous consequences will follow, but in c"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "45665183841e4edeaf06edbeaeed529e_107",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "What is or not negligent involves a consideration of that which a reasonable man would or not would not have done in the circumstances."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8df3106ae84c498f900e14e6fac03000_108",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This does not invariably rule out of consideration of subjective factors such as a person's knowledge, physical condition or age."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e2b50366e2864500a0e64888d6328110_109",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "25. In order to make out a case u/s 304A IPC against an accused, it is required to show that it was the accused who did some act which was rash or negligent; that act resulted in death CR No. 219 2023 Audhesh Kumar Pandey Vs State CR No. 22"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0b6b18bbeb774d58b3be9c3d15275a1a_110",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Thus, the prime requirement for invoking Section 304A against an accused is to show that it was he who had committed rash and negligent act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f897e2bfa2774017904a51d49516800b_111",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Connecting the accused with the rash and negligent act is of vital importance in a case u/s 304A IPC.\n26."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "584b409e51d64bf991612bd17d5edd7d_112",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Coming to the facts of the present case, although, there is ample evidence on record to show that the responsibility of maintenance at the place of incident was of the maintenance company M/s JLL."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "af439ef950ff4a849bd062142efa9973_113",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nThere is also prima facie evidence to show that the incident had occurred due to the breach of duty of M/s JLL in maintaining the safety and security of the place of incident to avoid any untoward Audhesh Kumar Pandey vs State on 28 May, 2"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e5e53c8cab66453fa08d52f0086b1841_114",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Since, the breach of duty of M/s JLL in maintaining the site has resulted in demise of a person, the same can also be characterised as gross negligence as required for attracting the offence u/s 304A IPC."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "411d3f2e765a49b5849ac3e794e5517d_115",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "However, it is a fact that the company M/s JLL has not been impleaded as an accused in the present case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "764c630dc23a44be9d3729910b23d328_116",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The revisionists herein are chargesheeted as accused persons merely on account of their designation as Directors in the maintenance company M/s JLL."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1c0f8c7533ba465bb9c7beadad049dec_117",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "A bare perusal of the chargesheet clearly show that the only reason given for impleading the revisionists herein as accused persons in the present FIR is the fact that they were Directors of JLL."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7e1ed46733dc405d9b9d007343a7437f_118",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "No overt or covert act of negligence has been attributed to them in the entire chargesheet."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0cf2eacfcea94928901bc419cc4893ba_119",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The investigation has not revealed their presence at the place of incident at the time of incident."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d6e3f77598b6461daf561a98669dfd12_120",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is also amply clear from the chargesheet that Revisionist Audhesh Kumar Pandey is based in Gurgaon, revisionist Ravinder Kumar CR No. 2192023 Audhesh Kumar Pandey Vs State CR No. 2202023 Ravinder Dhiman Vs State Dhiman is based in Mumbai"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "867701080e304b04b6006b538a8f3341_121",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is not the case of the IO that any of these revisionists had visited and personally checked safety and security of the place of incident."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e22ea3d7ecc6449ca34c83aaa1f4cc2c_122",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "No vicarious liability in such circumstances is recognised in criminal law."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "984492be90f74181bb3404853b58f324_123",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This is more so in the present case as the maintenance company itself (JLL) has not been made an accused."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "cb0442dccdc140e78b85d0713a7df5b7_124",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Perusal of the entire charge-sheet clearly shows that there is no evidence on record to show any rash or negligent act at the hands of the revisionists herein which is sufficient to put them to trial in the present FIR."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e3ef415de999470db855ea92e2ef7d19_125",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Moreover, attracting the provision u/s 34 IPC in the facts and circumstances of the case is beyond the scope of Section 34 IPC itself."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "97b1fdbe79824e0aa7faf836eb077566_126",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "No common intention to commit a rash and negligent act resulting in the reported accident can be imputed on the revisionists."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5731ff76f7cb42acb9c891d99b14490e_127",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Accordingly, it is not proper to prosecute the revisionists herein by attracting Section 34 IPC against them."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "192f68f1ee844b0ba3fd7ecaa5c0c3e3_128",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is a settled law that summoning of an accused is a serious order which entails a number of legal consequences and same should not be passed in a casual manner."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a5b8a290dd6d493c80a59bde1ae6992f_129",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Court has to be prima facie convinced that there is sufficient incriminating material for proceeding against an accused before summoning him for trial."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "72eed0e34e634d31be3d00801d9d5604_130",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This is all in the cases whether an accused has been chargesheeted or not chargesheeted by the IO."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "00a126f8b87e405a8d96a768e8a1e814_131",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "27. In view of the reasons given above and considering the material available on record, I am of the opinion that impugned order dated 02.06.2022 suffers from infirmity and illegality as it has directed summoning of the revisionists herein "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "73e96a5cb6e54e5c9793a5a3e62b7141_132",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Ld. Trial Court has CR No. 2192023 Audhesh Kumar Pandey Vs State CR No. 2202023 Ravinder Dhiman Vs State committed error of law by summoning the accused no. 1, 2 and 3 i.e. Revisionists herein merely because they have been chargesheeted by "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "323675d7e6844b27952e56d94f842646_133",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc",
        "explicit_leakage_phrase"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bset\\s+aside\\b",
          "matched_text": "set aside",
          "start": 216,
          "end": 225
        }
      ],
      "text_preview": "Accordingly, the present revision petitions are allowed and the impugned order dated 02.06.2022 qua the summoning of accused Audhesh Kumar Pandey, Ravinder Kumar Dhiman and Rahul Jain i.e. the revisionists herein is set aside."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4809116515b64b10a5563bb1f728a01b_134",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
